{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:a1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin with, you should choose your destination and calculate the distance."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps the implicit process start and the explicit first action to the corresponding source unit."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "branch:b1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "While doing so, continue to check if you need to book a train or a flight."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the decision point for choosing transport mode."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->a3",
        "action:a3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the answer is \"no\", then proceed to book a train."
      ],
      "justification": "Routes to the train-booking action based on the decision outcome. Variable naming preserves the logical flow."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->a4",
        "action:a4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the answer is \"yes\", then book a flight."
      ],
      "justification": "Routes to the flight-booking action based on the alternative decision outcome."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2t->a5t",
        "guard:b2f->a5f",
        "action:a5t",
        "action:a5f"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available within 24 hours, the process will end."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the 24-hour time check and immediate termination. Duplication across t/f paths is redundant but behavior-preserving."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2t->a6t",
        "guard:b2f->a6f",
        "action:a6t",
        "action:a6f"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if 24 hours have passed, you should call a travel agency."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the fallback path when 24 hours pass, including the required agency call."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3t->a7t",
        "guard:b3f->a7f",
        "action:a7t",
        "action:a7f"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available, the process will end along with the hotel reservation."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the code-availability check leading to process termination and hotel reservation handling."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3t->a8t",
        "guard:b3f->a8f",
        "action:a8t",
        "action:a8f"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if a code is not available, you should cancel your journey. In that case, the process will end as well."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the cancellation step and final process termination when no code is found. Multiple end nodes are structural plumbing for the stated terminations."
    }
  ],
